  "summaries": {
    "en": "Octopath Traveler: Champions of the Continent guide—Break system mastery, traveler party construction, and Guild battles.",
    "ja": "オクトパストラベラー 大陸の覇者攻略。ブレイクシステム制覇・旅人パーティ構成・ギルドバトルを解説。"
  },
  "category": "jrpg",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "The Break system (identical to the mainline game) requires hitting enemy weaknesses (weapons and magic types) to reduce the Shield gauge to 0; Breaking applies a 1.5x damage multiplier for one full turn.",
      "Party construction requires covering all 8 weapon types and 6 magic elements across 4 active characters; achieving \"full Break coverage\" guarantees breaking any non-immune enemy in 2–3 attack rounds.",
      "Boost (BP) management is the strategic layer beneath Breaking—accumulate 5 BP per character maximum, then spend 3–4 BP in a single turn post-Break to maximize burst damage in the Break window.",
      "Travel Bingo provides the primary ruby (premium currency) income outside of events; completing Bingo rows daily compounds into significant pull frequency over monthly periods.",
      "Guild content requires coordination with 29 other players for weekly Guild Battle bosses; joining an active guild that coordinates job assignments dramatically increases Guild Battle score."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "ブレイクシステム（本家ゲームと同一）は敵の弱点（武器と魔法タイプ）を当ててシールドゲージを0にする必要がある。ブレイクすると1ターン全体で1.5倍ダメージ乗数が適用される。",
      "パーティ構築は4人のアクティブキャラクター全体で8種類の武器タイプと6種類の魔法属性をカバーする必要がある。「完全ブレイクカバレッジ」を達成すると免疫でない敵を2〜3攻撃ラウンドで確実にブレイクできる。",
      "ブースト（BP）管理がブレイクの下にある戦略的レイヤー。キャラクターあたり最大5BPを蓄積し、ブレイクウィンドウのバーストダメージを最大化するためにブレイク後の1ターンに3〜4BPを使う。",
      "トラベルビンゴはイベント外の主要なルビー（プレミアム通貨）収入を提供する。毎日ビンゴ行を完了することで月次期間にわたって大きなプル頻度に積み重なる。",
      "ギルドコンテンツは毎週のギルドバトルボスのために他の29人のプレイヤーとの調整が必要。ジョブ割り当てを調整するアクティブなギルドに参加するとギルドバトルスコアが劇的に向上する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Break System Fundamentals",
        "body": "Begin by learning the weapon and magic weakness system. Each enemy has a fixed set of weaknesses (typically 4–6 from the 14 possible types); the Shield count reduces by 1 per weakness hit. For story content, identify the most common enemy archetypes for each chapter's region and build a party specifically covering those weakness categories. The Thief, Hunter, and Cleric classes from the first continent provide solid early-game Break coverage for most enemy types encountered through Chapter 3."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Advanced Job Assignment",
        "body": "Mid-game content introduces Advanced Jobs (Armsmaster, Inventor, etc.) that provide unique passive abilities and support skills not available in base jobs. The Armsmaster job (available from Chapter 4 continent) enables equipping multiple weapon types simultaneously, dramatically improving single-character Break coverage. Build one \"Break anchor\" character with Armsmaster and fill the remaining three party slots with high-damage boosted characters for optimal burst rotation."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Sacred Beasts and Guild Battles",
        "body": "Sacred Beast fights (optional postgame bosses equivalent to the main game's Galdera fight) require teams specialized for extended multi-phase battles with rotating elemental immunities. Guild Battles use the same combat system but against standardized boss configurations shared by all guilds; studying the weekly boss weakness rotation and pre-planning job assignments with guild members before the battle window opens produces the highest aggregate scores."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Not tracking enemy weaknesses before combat—every enemy in CotC has a discoverable weakness set; using Scout skills (e.g., Eye of the Inquisitor) before combat reveals all weaknesses at the cost of 1 action, which is almost always worth the trade.",
      "Spending BP outside of Break windows—BP spent on non-broken enemies wastes 33% of maximum possible damage output; discipline about saving BP for Break windows is the single most impactful habit in CotC combat.",
      "Building parties without full elemental coverage—a party missing even one element type will encounter enemies immune to all other party elements, requiring retreating to adjust composition.",
      "Not maintaining daily Bingo and Adventure goals—these two daily systems together provide 90%+ of free ruby income; missing even 3 days per week represents significant pull frequency loss.",
      "Investing in 3-star characters when 4-star and 5-star are available—character investment is expensive in CotC; always verify if a 5-star alternative with equivalent role exists before committing upgrade materials to a 3-star unit."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "戦闘前に敵の弱点を追跡しない。CotCの全ての敵は発見可能な弱点セットを持つ。戦闘前にスカウトスキル（異端審問者の目など）を使うと1アクションのコストで全弱点が明らかになる。これはほぼ常に価値のあるトレード。",
      "ブレイクウィンドウ外でBPを使う。ブレイクされていない敵に使ったBPは最大可能ダメージ出力の33%を無駄にする。ブレイクウィンドウのためにBPを節約することはCotC戦闘で最も影響力のある単一の習慣。",
      "完全な属性カバレッジなしでパーティを構築する。1つの属性タイプすら欠けているパーティは他の全てのパーティ属性に免疫な敵に遭遇し、構成を調整するために撤退が必要になる。",
      "毎日のビンゴとアドベンチャーゴールを維持しない。これら2つの毎日のシステムが一緒に無料のルビー収入の90%以上を提供する。週に3日でも逃すと大きなプル頻度の損失になる。",
      "4星と5星が利用可能な時に3星キャラクターに投資する。CotCではキャラクター投資が高価。同等の役割を持つ5星の代替品が存在するかどうかを常に確認してから3星ユニットにアップグレード素材をコミットする。"
    ]
  },
